---
import AboutHeroImage from "../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg";
import Layout from "../layouts/BlogPost.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About Me"
  description="Sylvia's programming journey"
  pubDate={new Date("September 07 2026")}
  heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
  <h3>Career Timeline</h3>
  <div class="timeline">
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2026</span><span class="desc"
        >Looking for work! Contact me if you're interested :)</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2023</span><span class="desc"
        >Co-Founder &amp; CTO at Searchless Inc.</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2022</span><span class="desc"
        >Software Engineer at Dropbox, working on their core storage team</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2020</span><span class="desc"
        >Software Engineer at Amazon, working on Alexa</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2019</span><span class="desc"
        >Software Developer at Jonah Group</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2019</span><span class="desc"
        >Graduated from the University of Toronto with an HBSc in Physics and
        Computer Science</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2018</span><span class="desc"
        >Various contracts while I finished my final year of university</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2017</span><span class="desc"
        >Took a year off school to work as an Embedded Software Engineer Intern
        at Verity</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2016</span><span class="desc"
        >Summer contract at UofT to improve their lab grading software</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2015</span><span class="desc"
        >I liked first year Physics courses, so started a second major</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2014</span><span class="desc"
        >Attended the University of Toronto for Computer Science</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2012</span><span class="desc"
        >Started working part time building Android and iOS apps</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2011</span><span class="desc"
        >Started taking online uni courses</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2007</span><span class="desc"
        >Started learning ActionScript so I could turn my Flash animations into
        games</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">2002</span><span class="desc"
        >Started learning HTML so I could plagiarize content from my bug books</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">1999</span><span class="desc"
        >Learned how to type "W I N [enter]" in DOS so I can play in Windows 3.1</span
      >
    </div>
    <div class="timeline-row">
      <span class="year">1996</span><span class="desc">Hello, world</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class="sub-heading">LARP Bio</h3>
  <div class="larp-bio">
    <h4>Background</h4>
    <p>
      Sylwia "Żmija Zygzakowata" Mirecka is a rogue from the Polish-Lithuanian
      Commonwealth of noble blood (Szlachta). Her father is the petty lord of
      the small village of Mircze in the Lublin Voivodeship (Województwo
      Lubelskie).
    </p>
    <p>
      Her mother was betroshed to Sylwia's father from a lord in The Kingdom of
      Scotland. Sylwia ran away from home when before her wedding - she didn't
      like the idea of being married off to a landlord in Bohemia for a sack of
      gold!
    </p>

    <p>
      It's not known exactly how Sylwia survives as a vegabond, but it's
      rumoured that she accepts legally-questionable contracts.
    </p>

    <h4>Aliases</h4>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Slavic areas:</strong> Sylwia "Żmija Zygzakowata" Mirecka</li>
      <li><strong>Germanic regions:</strong> Sylvia von Mirtzsche</li>
      <li><strong>Latin world:</strong> Silvia de Mircia / Silvia Mirczeska</li>
      <li><strong>British Isles:</strong> Sylvia "The Adder" of Mirche</li>
      <li>
        <strong>The Americas:</strong> Sylvia "Scorpion" Mirecki / Silvia "el Áspid"
        de Mirche
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h4>Catch Phrases</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>"Strzeż się Żmii!"</li>
      <li>"Ein Biss genügt"</li>
      <li>"Unter den Rosen schläft die Natter"</li>
      <li>"Hasta la vista, milord"</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Geographical Context</h4>
    <img
      src="/images/misc/plc_1634_map.jpg"
      alt="PLC 1632 Map"
      style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 1em;"
    />
  </div>

  <h3 class="sub-heading">Licenses</h3>
  <p>
    The written works on this website, excluding source code, are licensed under
    the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank"
      >Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License</a
    >
  </p>

  <p>
    Source code both in blog posts and on the public Git repository are licensed
    under the <a
      href="https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Licensing/BSD_with_Attribution"
      target="_blank">BSD with Attribution License</a
    >:
  </p>

  <pre
    class="license">
 Redistribution and use in source and binary forms, with or without
 modification, are permitted provided that the following conditions
 are met:

 1. Redistributions of source code must retain the above copyright
    notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer.

 2. Redistributions in binary form must reproduce the above copyright
    notice, this list of conditions and the following disclaimer in
    the documentation and/or other materials provided with the
    distribution.

 3. Neither the name of the copyright holder nor the names of its
    contributors may be used to endorse or promote products derived
    from this software without specific prior written permission.

 4. Redistributions of any form whatsoever must retain the following
    acknowledgment: 'This product includes software developed by 
    "Sylvia Mirecki" (https://sylviasshrubbery.ca/).'
    

